# The nasal vowels.
#
# Polish has two, ą and ę, and no module has either. What makes them possible
# without inventing any synthesis is nasalize_vow in us_filtr.dr: the engine
# already nasalises a vowel that stands next to a nasal consonant, and it does
# it by writing one global -- a frequency taken from another and raised by 150.
# So a nasal vowel is a vowel whose own rule writes that global without waiting
# for a consonant to follow.
#
# ę is the close-mid o's code, which nothing produces any more since every
# Polish o is the open one; its rule carries ɛ's formants and the nasalisation.
# ą had no code to take, so it has one of its own, and rather than copy five
# hundred lines of the open o's rule it uses that rule and these two decide
# whether to nasalise.

# Whether the phone about to be spoken is the one ą lays down. The scan is
# already at it where this is called from, which is the same place the value
# chain tests every other phoneme.
rule pol_test_aogonek takes 1 from is_sival.obj
  bare
  call test_string_s 2 1 sym pol_ph_aogonek
end

# And the nasalisation itself, which the open o's rule now asks for. It sets
# the scan for itself, since the rule it is called from has not set it yet.
rule pol_nasal_if_aogonek takes 1 from is_sival.obj
  bare
  call ZZlpta_load_vvg__setscan_0103r__2
  call test_string_s 2 1 sym pol_ph_aogonek
  if answer is not 0
    answer 0
  end
  raw load movl state 0 into r6
  raw load movw ind reg r6 2634 into r0w
  raw alu addw imm 150 reg r0w
  raw store movw reg r0w ind reg r6 2726
  answer 0
end
